  "body": "## Request\n\nAn agent or a script cannot get the full, typed list of the MCP tools of `camcraft-cli` without a running MCP session. The tools already carry input schemas, and their results already have `structuredContent`, but no command prints them.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Add `camcraft-cli mcp --schemas` (or `camcraft-cli commands --schemas`). It prints one JSON document: for each MCP tool, its name, description, input schema and, where known, output schema. Then it exits.\n2. Add an `outputSchema` to the MCP tools whose `structuredContent` has a fixed shape, so a client knows the result shape before the call.\n3. A test pins that every registered tool appears in the output and that each schema is valid JSON Schema.\n\nDone means: `camcraft-cli mcp --schemas` lists every MCP tool with its schemas, pinned by a test.\n\nIdea from SolidCraft 0.51 (`solidcraft-cli commands --schemas`); our own implementation.\n",
